 In my experiences with OOA/OOD/OOI, inheritance is vastly overated. 
 I found that many mistakes and design ratholes were created by trying to
 use inheritance where it didn't belong.  I am comming to the belief that
 the OPPers have merged a couple of concepts together when they implemented
 the idea called objects.  I think a better future lies in the direction
 of type systems and functional notations.  don't ask me to explain more for
 a few more months :-) perhaps some of our european friends can elaborate.

